ars, royalty was back. The Prince and Princess of Wales stepping out on the red carpet, Prince William, the president of the British Academy of film and Television Arts sporting a black velvet tuxedo. White Kate promoting sustainability, restyling an Alexander McQueen gown she first wore to the BAFTAs in 2019. It`s Britain`s most glamorous night and the highlight was a special tribute to the late Queen Elizabeth led by Dame Helen Mirren.\par \par \uc2 HELEN MIRREN, ACTRESS: Cinema at its best does what her majesty did effortlessly, bring us together and unite us in a story.\par \par \uc2 MCLAUGHLIN (voiceover): The queen honored with a BAFTA in 2013 for her long-standing patronage of the arts.\par \par \uc2 MIRREN: Your majesty, you were our nation`s leading star.\par \par \uc2 MCLAUGHLIN (voiceover): The tribute bringing a rare public show of emotion from Prince William. Mirren, who won both a BAFTA and an Oscar for her portrayal of the queen, shared what the tribute meant to her.\par \par \uc2 MIRREN: You know, I`m Elizabethan, you know. She was there for my whole life.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 MIRREN: And so, her passing was, you know --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: It was massive, wasn`t it?\par \par \uc2 MIRREN: It was massive.\par \par \uc2 MCLAUGHLIN (voiceover): As for the awards a teaser for the possible Oscar favorites. Kerry Condon and Barry Keoghan of "Banshees of Inisherin" both took supporting actor categories.\par \par \uc2 BARRY KEOGHAN, ACTOR, "BANSHEES OF INISHERIN": For the kids that are dreaming to be something from the area that I came from, this is for you.\par \par \uc2 HUNTER (voiceover): Austin Butler continued his winning streak adding to his Golden Globe win by taking home best leading actor for "Elvis".\par \par \uc2 AUSTIN BUTLER, ACTOR, "ELVIS": This is amazing.\par \par \uc2 [08:20:00]\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: And the BAFTA goes to Cate Blanchett for "Tar".\par \par \uc2 HUNTER (voiceover): Ca