e me through the season. That`s less than half of a tank of oil.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: Tom, there are also local programs that people can turn to for help.\par \par \uc2 COSTELLO: You know, this is important, every state has Home Energy Assistance Programs, so if you have trouble paying your bill, and the bills are going to get expensive this winter, turn to those programs. And you might even check with your own utility company to see if they offer assistance. And by the way, if you can pay your bill, if it`s no problem, and you can round off, you know, most states offer that option, roundup your bill to help those in need, this may be the win or two offer an extra dollar to help those in need. Savannah?\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: Tom, it`s a great idea, round up. Tom, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: All right, 7:15 time to cut to the chase. You did not win the big prize in last night`s Powerball. But we got good news, nobody else won on the jackpot, once again on the rise. So let`s look at the latest number, $800 million. That`s the latest number. It`ll probably even go up from there. So if someone wins it, it would be the second largest Powerball jackpot of all time. The next drawing Saturday night, you got plenty of time to get your tickets. Start planning what you`re going to do with your dough. Yes, plenty of time.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: All right, let`s get a first check of the weather, Al is on the road this morning in Fort Myers Beach, Florida. \uc2 Sun\uc2  is coming up, a pretty shot there. Al, good morning.\par \par \uc2 AL ROKER, NBC NEWS ANCHOR: Hey, good morning, guys. And we`re here to lend a hand to this hard hit community, ground zero for Hurricane Ian, which hit a month ago tomorrow. We`ll talk about that in just a little bit. But let`s talk about the risk of for some more severe weather as we head down south, we`re talking Texas and parts of Oklahoma. Storm hazards today, wind gusts of up to 60 miles per hour, i