ent \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  met yesterday with the January 6 Committee. That closed door interview comes as the investigation is winding down. The panel held its last hearing on October 13 and subpoenaed Trump himself last week to testify next month.\par \par \uc2 Hicks served in multiple senior roles in Trump`s White House for much of his presidency. She left the job six days after the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: People who are recovering this morning after a fuel tanker caught fire yesterday on a busy stretch of interstate in South Florida. This was the scene that happened after a three vehicle crash in Delray Beach, a plume of thick black smoke that you see there. That plume of smoke could be seen from miles away. The highway was shut down both directions for several hours. The cause of the crash is still under investigation.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: OK. It`s common for parents to steer their kids away from video games and encourage them of course to go play outside instead. But the news is not all bad when it comes to gaming. So this is according to new research. And this is published in the medical journal.\par \par \uc2 The JAMA Network Open says this. Kids who play video games for three or more hours per day performed better on impulse control and memory tests than kids who do not play. Now previous research has linked video games with depression and aggressive behavior, but the latest study found that there were no significant differences in behavior.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: There are a lot of young kids right now listen to the TODAY SHOW getting ready to go to school who are saying right now. You see mom, I told you. I told you.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: I know.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: We turn now out to that growing scandal that`s engulfing the Miss USA pageant.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Yes. A winner was crowned earlier this month. But in the weeks that have followed, several contestants have come forward and they claim the competition was rigged.\par \par