ared his soul to the nation.\par \par \uc2 COBIELLA (voice-over): The new season is controversial because it will focus on \uc2 Prince Charles\uc2  and Princess Diana`s divorce as well as her death. In an open letter to the "Sunday Times," Oscar winning actress Dame Judi Dench calling on \uc2 Netflix\uc2  to place a disclaimer on the series, writing in part, the time has come for \uc2 Netflix\uc2  to reconsider for the sake of a family and a nation so recently bereaved.\par \par \uc2 Dench who describes herself as a great believer of artistic freedom, calling this series, cruelly unjust, adding, the closer the drama comes to our present times, the more freely it seems willing to blur the lines between historical accuracy and crude sensationalism. The Times disclosing despite Dench`s close relationship with the royal family, she has not been prompted to write the letter.\par \par \uc2 [07:35:05]\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I don`t often get into a fight. But when I do I want to win.\par \par \uc2 COBIELLA (voice-over): \uc2 Netflix\uc2  describes the series as a fictional dramatization inspired by real events. In a statement of variety, creator Peter Morgan responding to the recent criticism, writing in part about \uc2 King Charles\uc2  in the royal family, I have enormous sympathy for a man in his position, indeed, a family in their position. \uc2 Netflix\uc2  also confirming to The Sun this week that it will not show the exact moment of Diana`s death in the series. The two actors who portrayed Charles and Diana in the new season, defending the show amid the scrutiny.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: To a certain responsibility towards these characters.\par \par \uc2 COBIELLA (voice-over): Elizabeth Debicki who will play Diana also calling the amount of research and caretaking in the production, immense. Photos of Debicki and the upcoming seasons have gone viral recently with her striking portrayal of the people`s Princess. Matt Smith, who played Prince Phili