par \par \uc2 ROKER: Strawberry.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Strawberry.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: It`s good.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: Talk amongst yourselves.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: Are those toasted right now, you guys?\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Toasted. They smell good.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: Oh, gosh, yummy, yummy.\par \par \uc2 Coming up, the highlights from our special inspiring night with military caregivers, Tom Hanks, Elizabeth Dole, and really special reunion coming up, but first your local news and weather.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [07:56:11]\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and programming copyright 2022 NBCUniversal.  ALL RIGHTS   RESERVED. Transcription Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document TODA000020221020eiak000gp\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par {\*\bkmkstart toc70}{\*\bkmkend toc70}\b \uc2 The New Pledge From President Biden, If Democrats Keep Control Of Congress, He`ll Immediately Move To Pass National Abortion Rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Lester Holt, Sam Brock \par \uc2 702 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 October 2022\par \uc2 NBC News: Nightly News\par \uc2 NTLN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and programming copyright 2022 NBCUniversal. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Transcription Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 LESTER HOLT: 21 days before the Midterms, President Biden trying to keep abortion rights front and center, but polls show voters worrying most about the economy and soaring inflation. Peter Alexander reports on the new clashes between candidates in key battlegrounds.\par \par \uc2 [19:05:09]\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 PETER ALEXANDER, NBC NEWS CHIEF WHITE HOUSE CORRESPONDENT (voiceover): With just three weeks until the Midterms and Republicans slamming Democrats over the economy and record inflation, President Biden tonight trying to amplify the politically divisive issue of abortion rights, urging voters to keep Democrats in control of Congress.\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Here`s the promise I make to you and the American people. The first bill that I will send to the Congress will be to codify Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 ALEXANDER: But some Democrats fear the potency of that message may be waning. Tonight, a new poll shows 44 percent of likely voters cite the economy or inflation as the number one problem facing the country while just five percent list abortion as their top issue. And now, Republicans have a four-point lead when voters are asked which party`s candidate they`d support.\par \par \uc2 In Ohio, one of several crucial races that`ll determine control of the Senate. Republican candidate J.D. Vance hammered Democrat \uc2 Tim Ryan\uc2  over skyrocketing prices in a heated final debate.\par \par \uc2 J.D. VANCE (R-OH) SENATE CANDIDATE: That rising energy price that people see at the pump, that they see in the utility bills, that was the direct result of policies enacted by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  and supported 100 percent by \uc2 Tim Ryan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ALEXANDER: While Ryan slammed Vance for embracing former President Trump.\par \par \uc2 REP. TIM RYAN (D-OH): You were calling Trump America`s Hitler. Then he kissed his ass --\par \par \uc2 VANCE: It`s not true.\par \par \uc2 RYAN: It is true. And then you kissed his ass, and then he endorsed you. And you said he`s the greatest president of all time.\par \par \uc2 ALEXANDER: There are critical governor`s races too in the battlegrounds of Arizona and Michigan and a rematch in Georgia between Republican Governor \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  and Democrat \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2 . Their one and only showdown last night.\par \par \uc2 STACEY ABRAMS (D-GA), GUBERNATORIAL CANDIDATE: We live in a state of fear. And this is a governor who for the last four years has beat his chest but delivered very little for most Georgians.\par \par \uc2 ALEXANDER: Kemp touting his early moves to reopen the state during the pandemic and going after Abrams.\par \par \uc2 GOV. BRIAN KEMP (R-GA): Miss Abrams is going to lie out my record because she doesn`t want to talk about her own.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 HOLT: Peter, President Biden is going to pivot to the economy tomorrow focusing on high gas prices.\par \par \uc2 ALEXANDER (on camera): Yes, Lester, that`s right. Looking to lower those prices, the President is going to announce that the administration will move forward with the release of as many as 15 million additional barrels of oil from the Strategic Petroleum Reserve. It`s a controversial move that comes amid Russia`s war in Ukraine and after Saudi Arabia snub the President`s request to boost oil production. Lester?\par \par \uc2 HOLT: Peter Alexander at the White House, thank you.\par \par \uc2 There`s breaking news and a trial involving a murder they went unsolved for 25 years. A California man convicted late today for killing Kristin Smart, a college student who disappeared in 1996. Paul Flores, a former classmate of Smart`s wasn`t arrested for the crime until last year. Flores` father who was accused of helping move Smart`s body was found not guilty. Smart`s remains were never found.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Con