e company, but can even change based on individual franchises. What is clear is businesses have had to adjust the prices they charge with food and fuel costs jumping at least 8 or 9 percent due to inflation.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I think we`re definitely seeing pushback among lower middle income consumers as price hikes have been across the board in the quick service restaurants base this year starting to see more and more customers trade out and trade down to convenience stores, dollar stores, and other channels.\par \par \uc2 BROCK (voice-over): Chipotle has increased its prices four times since the summer of 2020. McDonald`s announcing a roughly 8 percent hike in the first quarter of this year, noting inflation is affecting all sectors and no one is immune. Though there are still value deals like the 1, 2, 3 dollar menu and \uc2 Taco Bell\uc2  gaining virality this week after a Fox Business contributor said this in the context of inflation.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT MARTIN, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Yesterday, yes, I had a nice lunch at \uc2 Taco Bell\uc2 , it cost me about $28.\par \par \uc2 BROCK (voice-over): The contributor roundly criticized and the company even responding on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , 14 times to $2 burritos equals $28. What`s your $28 order? But clearly not all the burritos are that inexpensive?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Just right now I was at \uc2 Taco Bell\uc2  and I asked for a burrito, regular burrito too, and it was 8.51 for the price.\par \par \uc2 BROCK (on camera): For one burrito.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 BROCK (voice-over): \uc2 Taco Bell\uc2  did not return a request for comment. Meanwhile, some fast food reward programs that many consumers love are also tightening their belts. \uc2 Dunkin Donuts\uc2  recently raised the cost of earning a free cup of coffee to $50 up from 40. While Chipotle did the same thing with its entrees going from $140 spent to more than 160 to earn a free burrito, whether it`s 