k that you really come up with that?\par \par \uc2 SHLESINGER: Yes. As just a joke, because I thought it was very funny to have like, hot young girls of saying the word, elder. And then, it became part of the zeitgeist. But I don`t care any royalties.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HAGER: You know, I`m an elder -- we are both Elder Millennial.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Yes.\par \par \uc2 SHLESINGER: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: And I miss the cut off to be whatever is above millennial, by one month.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Yes, by one month?\par \par \uc2 SHLESINGER: Oh, by one month.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Or age.\par \par \uc2 SHLESINGER: I`m not going to ask your age, but --\par \par \uc2 HAGER: I`m 40.\par \par \uc2 SHLESINGER: OK.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: I`m 41 in November.\par \par \uc2 SHLESINGER: OK, right there, technically, you can sit with us like because we`re very inclusive, because we`re like, kind of old now. But you are like young, young Gen X.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Oh.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Wait, what?\par \par \uc2 SHLESINGER: I`ll show myself out.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: That`s OK.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: No, wait, I just saw somebody shake their head. I`m a millennial. She said I`m a Millennial.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Wait, wait, well --\par \par \uc2 SHLESINGER: Now, you`re millennial.\par \par \uc2 It`s a -- it`s a -- it`s a blurred line. It`s a nebulous group.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Oh, but you can sit with them.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: OK, because actually, a lot of the things that you talk about in this book, but also on the Netflix`s special about nostalgia --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: We have the same shared reference.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: We do.\par \par \uc2 SHLESINGER: And also, we`re both from Dallas.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Yes.\par \par \uc2 SHLESINGER: And so --\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Don`t worry, it`s OK, baby.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: OK.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: I want to take a trip down there (INAUDIB