boards.\par \par \uc2 JONES: There you go.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: Let`s talk about the Latin Billboards here for a moment.\par \par \uc2 DEL CASTILLO: Oh, yes.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: Christina Aguilera performing.\par \par \uc2 DEL CASTILLO: Oh, my God.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: How was it?\par \par \uc2 DEL CASTILLO: That was -- I mean, I get goosebumps. Really, she was stunning. We all know she has an amazing voice. But hearing her cantar mariachi, like, for me was the most amazing thing in the entire night. It was a fun night. I love to host and she was unbelievable. And she sang with no accent with, you know, with this beautiful song. I love it. I love her.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: Her range is amazing.\par \par \uc2 DEL CASTILLO: Yes, yes.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: It really is.\par \par \uc2 DEL CASTILLO: That voice, oh, my God.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: And, Kate, talk about 180. You`re doing -- tell us about this comedy series you`re doing on Peacock.\par \par \uc2 DEL CASTILLO: I know. It`s our friends, you know, in Peacock.\par \par \uc2 MARTIN-BROOKS: Yes.\par \par \uc2 DEL CASTILLO: So, it`s really fun. It`s a dark comedy. And we Latinos are not used to doing a lot of dark comedy, but we are used to watching it a lot. So, let`s see how it goes. It started on Peacock, like, I don`t know, like probably two weeks ago and in HBO Max for Mexico and Latin America, the 29th, on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 JONES: Something new.\par \par \uc2 MARTIN-BROOKS: Yes.\par \par \uc2 DEL CASTILLO: So, it`s a completely different character from Teresa Mendoza. This is a fragile woman, you know, has no idea how to carry a gun or anything at all.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: Yes.\par \par \uc2 DEL CASTILLO: So, it`s really a lot of fun.\par \par \uc2 JONES: You get the full range.\par \par \uc2 MARTIN-BROOKS: I was going to say.\par \par \uc2 DEL CASTILLO: I`m trying to. I`m trying to.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: Very nice. Kate, thank you so much. Thanks for being here.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 DEL CASTILLO: Of course.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: "La Reina del Sur" premiers October 18th on our sister network, Telemundo.\par \par \uc2 JONES: All right. They`re still moving. They have been moving now for hours. Downstairs, when I walked in, they were moving. Coming up, we kicked off our October "Start TODAY" fitness plan this morning and Stephanie Mansour. She`s back to show us some moves to jazz up your daily walks.\par \par \uc2 And then, later, Jake Lacy is here to tell us about his new true crime series. A lot going on this morning. We`ll be right back.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [09:40:00]\par \par \uc2 ROKER: OK. So, we just started October and we want to kick off our brand- new "Start TODAY" walking club challenge sponsored by Easy Spirit. Our online community going strong. More than 100,000 members.\par \par \uc2 MARTIN-BROOKS: Wow.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: So, now, is the perfect time to join. Just scan the QR code on the screen. You can sign up for our "Start TODAY" newsletter to help you get daily motivation.\par \par \uc2 MARTIN-BROOKS: And you motivate us every morning to do this. And someone else who does, TODAY Fitness Contributor Stephanie Mansour leads our "Start TODAY" group. And she`s here with two members, Judy Bacani (ph) and Jennifer Lopez (ph), it must be --\par \par \uc2 ROKER: Wow.\par \par \uc2 MARTIN-BROOKS: Sorry. -- Rudy Bacani (ph) and Jennifer --\par \par \uc2 ROKER: And, Jennifer, you`re from the Bronx, too, right, aren`t you, Jennifer?\par \par \uc2 JENNIFER LOPEZ, START TODAY MEMBER: Yes.\par \par \uc2 MARTIN-BROOKS: And it must be easy to get reservations, right?\par \par \uc2 ROKER: Jenny from the Block. There you go.\par \par \uc2 MARTIN-BROOKS: All right. So, let`s get started here.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE MANSOUR, TODAY FITNESS CONTRIBUTOR: All right. So, for our October workout plan, we are including strength training. Now, we add this halfway through the month and that`s because, you know, our stretch routine last month was wildly successful. People loved the stretching. But I wanted to change it up a little bit.\par \par \uc2 So, while we include stretching in motion at the beginning of our walks to help us warm up our bodies because it`s getting chilly out, we also include that strength training for people that are looking to improve balance, improve their stability, walk with more power, walk faster, walk longer. And I am so excited that you guys are here because you have questions about this plan, right?\par \par \uc2 RUDY BACANI, START TODAY MEMBER (PH): Yes.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: Rudy, what`s your question for Step?\par \par \uc2 BACANI (PH): So, when I`m doing my shoulder exercises, I seem to get a little tension in my neck.\par \par \uc2 MANSOUR: Yes, in your neck. Yes.\par \par \uc2 BACANI (PH): Am I doing them incorrectly?\par \par \uc2 MANSOUR: That`s a great question. And that`s realty common actually too, guys, because when we are lifting weights, we want to make sure that we`re not using those traps, the trapezius muscles. So, I`m going to show you the side extension. Now, this is a lateral raise from our plant. So, we`re going to lift the weights up as high as the shoulders and then, lower them down. Good. And then, lift them up as high as your shoulders and lower them down. And keep going.\par \par \uc2 I want to make sure everyone sees here. We are not hunching up with the neck. So, if you were to lift those shoulders up really, really high and then, lift the weights, that`s why we get the neck tension and that pain. So, you want to make sure those traps are relaxed and we`re lifting only using the shoulders. And this is key, guys, only going as high as the shoulders. Don`t lift up higher than this or else you definitely will recruit those muscles in the neck. How does that feel?\par \par \uc2 MARTIN-BROOKS: Does that help?\par \par \uc2 BACANI (PH): Good.\par \par \uc2 MANSOUR: Good?\par \par \uc2 BACANI (PH): Much better.\par \par \uc2 MARTIN-B