ed by a predator, a master manipulator and how does that leave you on the fence when from outside you would go, I would do this, I would do that, why didn`t they do that? On the inside, you don`t know which way to turn and feel cornered. So, I hope that, you know, in this format we are able to dive into that a little more.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: You mentioned the real-life Jan Broberg is involved as a producer.\par \par \uc2 LACY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: I understand that she wrote you a letter before the production started.\par \par \uc2 LACY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: What did the letter say?\par \par \uc2 LACY: You know, the first half of his -- she left this wonderful note in my trailer on the first day of filming and the first half was about B and said like he was warm and charming and generous and a wonderful storyteller and that that was his superpower, was like to make you feel so included and so unique in his orbit. And then, the second half was a really just so gracious on her end to say, like, I`m in a good place. You can do this job.\par \par \uc2 JONES: You`re there.\par \par \uc2 LACY: You know, like, tell the story. Do your work. Like, you don`t have to be prioritizing like telling the story and then, also thinking, like, is Jan OK?\par \par \uc2 JONES: OK. Right.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: Yes.\par \par \uc2 JONES: Yes.\par \par \uc2 LACY: Are we retraumatizing her?\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: Good for her.\par \par \uc2 LACY: You know, it was like generous beyond something I could maybe ever - -\par \par \uc2 ROKER: Gave you permission.\par \par \uc2 JONES: Gave in the grace.\par \par \uc2 LACY: Yes, it was beautiful.\par \par \uc2 MARTIN-BROOKS: So, how would you prepare for a role like this, because we are used to seeing you, I mean, your "White Lotus" character, you know, sort of like this unlikable boyfriend? And now, you are playing a really serious role. So, the juxtaposition of those, how do you --\par \par \uc2 LACY: It`s a mix. You know, it`s a mix 