t going on and on about the properties and about money, about the company. And I said I`m not even asking for none of that stuff. I don`t want none of it.\par \par \uc2 CANNING (voice-over): Whichever version was true, the two women had never met because Hank told Bill he needed to break it off with Bonnie before something bad happened.\par \par \uc2 H. HALL: I said you need to get out of that relationship. Don`t turn back.\par \par \uc2 CANNING (on camera): Did you kind of feel like, hey, Bill, you`re playing with fire and --\par \par \uc2 H. HALL: It`s exactly what I told him. I said he needed to go fix this man. You know, fix your house. Frances threw him out. He went back to Bonnie and he would go back to begging Frances to go back. He`s very confused. I`ve never seen Bill like that, never in my life.\par \par \uc2 CANNING (voice-over): Frances was conflicted too, take Bill back or kick him out for good. The morning of October 9th, her anger boiled over.\par \par \uc2 F. HALL: He was brushing his teeth. And I glanced over and I just -- I was enraged.\par \par \uc2 CANNING (voice-over): She started pulling his hair, tousled with him all around the house. Bill appeared to take the assault as a joke.\par \par \uc2 F. HALL: He was doing these little dances, he does. And it upset me so much and I kicked him in he goes, stop already. I go, no.\par \par \uc2 CANNING (voice-over): She went after his prized possessions, knocking over his custom Harley Davidson and hitting their new Range Rover with a stick.\par \par \uc2 F. HALL: He pushed me down. I fell down. And he took off and waved at him, smiling.\par \par \uc2 CANNING (voice-over): The following day was rough for Frances. Her family coaxed her out of the house to watch her niece`s volleyball game. Then on her way home, driving her Cadillac Escalade.\par \par \uc2 F. HALL: And Bill in his bike. And back of Bill, I see the Range Rover. And I`m like, who is that?\par \par \uc2 CANNING (voice-over): The vehicles were 