ing.\par \par \uc2 CANNING (voice-over): She said Bonnie repeatedly slammed on the brakes, forcing Frances to slam on hers. Frances had a large slab of granite in the back of her Escalade from a home renovation project.\par \par \uc2 F. HALL: So I can hear this piece of granite every time I break because it moves.\par \par \uc2 CANNING (voice-over): As Bonnie accelerated, Frances stayed on her. It was as if she had developed tunnel vision, could focus on only one thing.\par \par \uc2 F. HALL: I`m going to confront her. I`m done. I`ve had it with her. I`m going to tell her, you want him, keep him.\par \par \uc2 CANNING (voice-over): The him in all of this, Bill, had been riding his motorcycle in front of Bonnie. But as the chase unfolded, he suddenly slowed down.\par \par \uc2 F. HALL: All this time Bill is in front of us. And I see Bill pulling over and she`s passing him.\par \par \uc2 CANNING (voice-over): Then Frances said, Bill dropped back to her right.\par \par \uc2 F. HALL: And I`m passing Bill. I see Bill from my passenger window, and she breaks and I brake, and I heard something, and I forgot to stop.\par \par \uc2 CANNING (voice-over): That piece of granite again, Frances thought. And she continued to chase after Bonnie still hell bent on confronting her. Suddenly Bonnie made a U turn. And as she makes a U turn. I make a U turn. She takes off.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I got a black Escalade and a black Range Rover. They`re traveling at a high rate of speed, I don`t know, 90, 100 miles an hour -- that black Range Rover was.\par \par \uc2 CANNING (voice-over): An off duty officer spotted Bonnie and Frances and called it in.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: They`re hauling ass -- driving on the wrong side of the road, acting like idiots.\par \par \uc2 CANNING (voice-over): Frances was still on Bonnie`s tail when --\par \par \uc2 F. HALL: I hear this wind coming in.\par \par \uc2 CANNING (voice-over): The howl of the wind snapped Frances out of her trance. She looked back and realized her third row passenger window was shattered. And then she realized something else. She couldn`t see Bill anywhere. Frances called her sister Connie who lived close by then she called her daughter Nikki.\par \par \uc2 N. HALL: She goes I can`t find your dad. I don`t know where your dad is. I`m turning around.\par \par \uc2 CANNING (voice-over): Frances started to make her way back down the highway. She spoke to Connie again.\par \par \uc2 F. HALL: My sister tells me I found him.\par \par \uc2 CANNING (voice-over): Connie had jumped in her own car and soon came upon Bill and his bike by the side of the road. He`d crashed and was in bad shape. Police were already at the scene when Frances arrived.\par \par \uc2 F. HALL: And into some running to him, an officer grabs me and they yank him. I heard somebody yelled, that`s his wife leave her alone. And I get down to where he`s at. And he`s alive.\par \par \uc2 CANNING (on camera): Do you say anything to him?\par \par \uc2 F. HALL: I was just in shock. And he kept telling me, I can`t breathe. And I told him calm down, dad. Calm down.\par \par \uc2 CANNING (voice-over): Bill had internal injuries. Whatever happened, the wreck was so severe that even knocked his boots off.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Sierra-4, here comes your bird.\par \par \uc2 CANNING (voice-over): They took him away in the helicopter?\par \par \uc2 F. HALL: They got a gurney and he grabbed my arm, and he goes, vieja, come with me. I go, I`m coming dad. And they take him and I remember he told them, she needs to come with me.\par \par \uc2 CANNING (voice-over): But officers wouldn`t allow Frances in the chopper, wouldn`t allow her to go anywhere in fact.\par \par \uc2 F. HALL: And I told the officer, I`m his wife, and he said turn around and he handcuffed me, put in the back, and they`ve left with Bill.\par \par \uc2 CANNING (voice-over): It was only then, Frances says, that it all came together in her mind. The thump,